 "equations": [],
 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Clamping",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "Below VRWM the diode draws at most IR. Past VBR it conducts hard, and during a surge the voltage across it rises to VC at the peak pulse current IPP. Forward, it behaves as an ordinary diode, 1.1 V max at 10 mA."
  },
  {
   "topic": "ESD clamping waveform",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "For ESD5Z5.0T1G under an 8 kV contact discharge, a positive strike leaves a spike of about 37 V lasting a few nanoseconds, then the voltage sits near 15 V to 20 V for some 30 ns, eases to about 7 V to 8 V and holds there until roughly 260 ns after the strike, when it drops to near zero. A negative strike spikes to about −31 V and recovers to within a few volts of zero in roughly 60 ns."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Surge waveform",
   "page": 4,
   "text": "Surge ratings use an 8/20 µs current pulse: the current reaches its peak IRSM at 8 µs and has decayed to half of it at 20 µs. The pulse width tP is measured to the half-value point."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Variants",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "T1G parts ship 3000 to a reel and T5G parts 8000. The SZ prefix marks versions for automotive and other uses needing site and change control, AEC-Q101 qualified and PPAP capable. All are lead-free and RoHS compliant."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Construction and assembly",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Void-free transfer-moulded thermoset body with UL 94 V-0 epoxy; leads finished in 100 % matte tin. Any mounting orientation. Peak reflow 260 °C; moisture sensitivity level 1. Body 1.20 mm × 0.80 mm, 0.7 mm high."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Marking",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "The top carries a two-letter device code (ZD, ZE, ZF, ZG, ZH or ZM), a date code M, and a lead-free indicator G that can be a microdot in either position. The date code orientation depends on the assembly site. The polarity band is at pin 1, the cathode."
  }
 ],
